{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nscarlet-unsocial-limpkin (Gerrit 3500, `8469f0a5ede`) added `_may_be_closed` and `_sets_closed` to `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`. Its LLM review left 2 advisory findings:\n- `_sets_closed` calls `.get` on `event[\"data\"]` and `data[\"fields\"]` without checking they are dicts. A raw event whose `data` or `fields` is a non-empty string or list raises `AttributeError`. That happens inside `_scoped_state`'s `except` handler, so `rebar verify-opcert` crashes with a traceback instead of judging the ticket. A crash exits non-zero (so the gate does not pass), but the operator gets a traceback, not a named ticket.\n- No test drives 3 of `_may_be_closed`'s \"may be closed\" branches: an event file that does not parse, JSON that is not an object, and a ticket directory with no active event files.\n\nReproducing it showed 2 more crash sites on the same malformed input, both before `_sets_closed` is reached: `_close_anchor_event` (`src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`) calls `(ev.event.get(\"data\") or {}).get(\"status\")`, so a STATUS whose `data` is a string raises; and `_event_from_file` (`src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py`, used by the merged-log walk `_collect_all` for both `verify-opcert` and `verify-identity`) calls `event.get(...)` on parsed JSON, so a file holding a JSON list raises. Review and a local fuzz (every event kind times 11 malformed `data` shapes, plus non-object and odd `event_type` files, with and without a failing reduce: 168 cases) found 2 more in `verify_authorship.py`: `_ledger_events` chains `.get` through a SNAPSHOT's `data` and `compiled_state`, and `_event_from_file` tests `event.get(\"event_type\") not in KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES`, which raises `TypeError` when `event_type` is a list.\n\n## Approach\n\n- `_sets_closed`: a non-dict `data` or `fields` returns True (\"may be closed\"), so the ticket is judged.\n- `_close_anchor_event`: skip an event whose `data` is not a dict (it cannot be a close anchor; a missing anchor is already enforced).\n- `_event_from_file`: return `[]` for parsed JSON that is not an object, exactly as it already does for unparseable JSON, and for an `event_type` that is not a string (it cannot be a known type). That keeps `verify-identity`'s handling of such a file identical to an unparseable one, which it already tolerates.\n- `_ledger_events`: read `data` and `compiled_state` with type checks, returning no ledger entries when either is not an object. Add tests for the 4 cases in `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`, reusing `_write_event` (extended to write raw text) and `_break_show_ticket`.\n\nNo config key, env var or flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`\n- `src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`\n\n## Testing\n\nWith `show_ticket` raising for an in-progress ticket and `--require-environment` set, each of these makes the gate exit 1 and report `unreadable ticket state` for it: an event file holding invalid JSON; a file holding a JSON list; a ticket directory whose only files are retired (`.json.retired`); a STATUS event whose `data` is a string. The STATUS-data-string, EDIT-fields-list, JSON-list, SNAPSHOT-data-string, SNAPSHOT-compiled-state-list and event-type-list cases raise against `8469f0a5ede`; each is a parametrized case of `test_malformed_raw_event_is_judged_not_a_crash`. Existing `verify-identity`/`verify-authorship` tests must still pass. Then `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A raw event whose `data` or `fields` is not an object no longer crashes `rebar verify-opcert`; the ticket is judged and reported `unreadable ticket state`: shown by a test that fails on `8469f0a5ede`.\n- [x] Tests cover an unparseable event file, a non-object JSON file and a directory with no active event files, each judged (exit 1 with a required environment).\n- [x] The existing `verify-opcert` and `verify-authorship`/`verify-identity` unit tests pass unchanged.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`, and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795344632546773001,"uuid":"dadfaaa2-7584-45fe-9fb0-729f8609fce2"}